    "title": "Man in Willimantic slashed a person's head with a kitchen knife, police say - NewsBreak",
    "text": "WILLIMANTIC — A man was arrested Wednesday after he slashed another person in the head with a knife, police say. Alberto Hernandez, 49, was charged with first-degree assault, carrying a dangerous weapon and breach of peace, Willimantic Police Lt. Joshua Clark said in a news release. Clark said officers were called to North Street at 2:40 p.m. for a report of an assault. He said arriving officers found one person with injuries that were not life-threatening and provided them with medical assistance. Clark said officers determined that Hernandez got into an argument with the victim, brandished a large kitchen knife and slashed them on the right side of their head. He said Hernandez attempted to flee the scene, but was quickly tracked down by responding officers and taken into custody. The victim was transported to Windham Hospital for treatment of head wounds and was released a couple of hours later, Clark said. Hernandez is being held in lieu of a $250,000 bond, Clark said. Sign up for CT Insider newsletters here Read the original article on ctinsider.com",
